The reply path with everything encoded: RFC 2047 encoded-words in Subject and From, a
folded Subject header, and a quoted-printable body carrying =C3=A9 =C3=B8 =C5=A1 =C2=A7
=E2=80=94.

05-encoded-headers.eml proves the parser decodes an incoming mail. This proves the same on
resume, which is a different code path in one respect that matters: `mailSubject` and
`mailSender` are overwritten on the waiting execution, so a resume that decodes badly
corrupts a case that was already correct.

Note that `References` is plain ASCII even here. Message-IDs are never encoded, which is
what keeps correlation working regardless of what the rest of the headers do.
